# vendored ML assets for the opt-in Rampart layer (~90 MB binaries; reproduce with
# tools/vendor_rampart.sh — kept out of source like the runtime data)
site/vendor/
site/models/
# the offline finding index — droplet-generated from the live corpus (~4.6 MB / 0.9 MB gz),
# like cards.jsonl. Reproduce with tools/build_offline_index.py; never committed.
site/search-index.json

# Personal data written by the companion modules — NEVER committed.
# binding = public keys + thread ids; deferred = what someone handed forward;
# bookofdays = a person's private record. These are theirs, not ours (docs/THE_COMPANION.md §6a).
data/bindings/
data/deferred/
data/bookofdays/
# The Fellowship Mesh — nodes (pubkey + callsign, no PII) and the relay's message queue are the
# believers' own, held in data/mesh/. A seized server yields only the public corpus (docs/THE_COMPANION.md §6a).
data/mesh/
# Web Push — the VAPID server key (a secret) and each node's push subscriptions (theirs, no PII).
data/push/
# The Works — the technical volume is COMPILED from the engine (real runs + minted seals),
# like the codex; the demonstrations' source is compendium.py, the sealed output is generated.
data/compendium/
data/codex/
# corpus backups + bulk reference data belong beside the engine, not in source
data/*.bak
data/cards.jsonl.*
data/easton/
data/herbs/
data/apothecary_proposals/
